<!DOCTYPE HTML>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<title>Rose+Co</title>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
		<link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/main.css" />
		<noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="assets/css/noscript.css" /></noscript>
		<link
		rel="icon"
		type="image/png"
		sizes="32x32"
		alt="Rose+Co"
		href="https://res.cloudinary.com/aliapurplejello/image/upload/v1667323919/rose-and-co-light_vjskbs.png"
	  />
	</head>
	<body class="landing is-preload">

		<!-- Page Wrapper -->
			<div id="page-wrapper">

				<!-- Banner -->
					<section id="banner">
						<div class="inner">
							<h2>Rose+Co</h2>
							<p>The Hair Stylist's Memory Bank</p>
							<ul class="actions special">
								<li><a href="/login" class="button primary">Sign In</a></li>
								<li><a href="/signup" class="button fit">New Account</a></li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

									<!-- One -->
									<section id="one" class="wrapper style1 special">
										<div class="inner">
											<header class="major">

												<h2 id="home-medium-heading">Track your client formulas, haircuts, spark notes, and pictures all in one place.</h2>
											</header>
											<ul class="features">
                       
												<li class="icon solid fa-keyboard">
                          
													<h3>Formulas at Your Fingertips</h3>
													<p>Add new formulas as your client's hair color desires change. Through your client formula cards on the app, you'll have the ability to see previous color formulas and haircut history.</p>
												</li>
												<li class="icon solid fa-comment">
													<h3>Eliminate the need to ask another stylist for a color formula</h3>
													<p>Fitting in another stylist's client? Now you can see their formula from the salon database in your Rose+Co app on the "Salon Clients" page.</p>
												</li>
												<li class="icon solid fa-clock">
													<h3>Cut down on your color mixing time</h3>
													<p>Your client formula cards are available all in one place to easily look up formulas, haircut details, and spark notes. Now you can get back to coloring hair sooner instead of trying to find what formula you used last time.</p>
												</li>
												<li class="icon solid fa-star">
													<h3>Remember every important detail of your client</h3>
													<p>Whether it be an important life update or changing a hair style - you can record every detail that matters to you here</p>
												</li>
											
												</li>
											</ul>
										</div>
									</section>

				<!-- Two -->
					<section id="two" class="wrapper style2 special">
						<div class="inner">
							
							<h2>Preview the Rose+Co App</h2>
								
						<div class="video-container">
							<video controls>
								<source src="https://res.cloudinary.com/aliapurplejello/video/upload/v1669140342/ScreenRecordingLightMode_z2x8xj.mp4" type="video/mp4">
								</video>
							</div>
						</div>
					</section>

				<!-- Three -->
					<section id="three" class="wrapper alt style2">
						<section class="spotlight">
							<div class="image"><img src="images/pic01.png" alt="Preview of 'My Clients' page on Mac" /></div><div class="content">
								<h2>My Clients</h2>
								<p>On this page, you can find all of your client cards in one place for a quick lookup of their formula. Clicking on their card will pull up a more detailed view that includes any updated formulas with dates of previous visits and spark notes.</p>
							</div>
						</section>
						<section class="spotlight">
							<div class="image"><img src="images/pic02.png" alt="Preview of 'Salon Clients' page on Mac" /></div><div class="content">
								<h2>Salon Clients</h2>
								<p>Here you will find a list of every client that is in the salon's database. Quickly look up formula and hair cut details. Can see who the client's regular hair stylist is. Clicking on their picture will pull up their full client card with every detail.</p>
							</div>
						</section>
						
					</section>



				<!-- CTA -->
					<section id="cta" class="wrapper style4">
						<div class="inner">
							<header>
								<h2>Get started</h2>
								<p>Discover how organized client information will make your days easier.</p>
							</header>
							<ul class="actions stacked">
								<li><a href="/login" class="button fit primary">Sign In</a></li>
								<li><a href="/signup" class="button fit">New Account</a></li>
							</ul>
						</div>
					</section>

			</div>

			<%- include('partials/footer') -%>